{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"IMPORTANT — THE STALE 1727 WAS SUBMITTED DURING THE PAUSE. The defect is live on main.\n\nOn resume I found both changes already merged:\n  e0a55d5fac  Sweep compaction out of band on a schedule\n  d2dea317ec  Trigger compaction from the close, out of band\n\nd2dea317ec is revision f34549d099 — the STALE one my standdown comment flagged. All five\nadvisory defects are on main right now; I verified each against the merged tree rather than\nassuming:\n\n- `compact_trigger.run_sweep` still has `record_sweep(tracker)` in its `finally`.\n- `.github/workflows/compact-sweep.yml:150` still pipes through `tee` under pipefail.\n- `transition_close.py:503,516` still say \"Compaction is NOT run here\" and \"DEDICATED CLONE\".\n\nPROVEN, not inferred: I checked out main's `compact_trigger.py` over my tree and ran my\nstand-aside test against it — it FAILS (\"standing aside stamped the sweep clock\"). Restoring my\nversion makes it pass. So the live defect is exactly the one the review named.\n\nWhy this matters more than it did an hour ago: RECONCILE_CONTINUOUS was turned off during the\nwindow, so the scheduled sweep plus this operation-linked trigger are now the store's ENTIRE\ncompaction story. The failure mode has nothing behind it — under sustained contention every\ntrigger stands aside, stamps the clock, and goes quiet, and the store stops compacting while\nits own freshness signal says it is healthy.\n\nFIX FORWARD (a revert would take the whole floor out with it). New change on top of current\nmain carrying only the delta between the stale revision and my corrected commit — extracted as\na patch from `git diff f34549d099 8bfe41b9e2` rather than re-typed, so it cannot drift from\nwhat the review actually asked for. Applied cleanly to all five files.\n\n  8fd5166a7b  Only stamp the sweep clock when a sweep ran\n\nLocal so far: 31 affected tests pass, ruff clean, mypy 526 files, complexity ratchet unchanged.\nBoth full tiers running now; pushing as soon as they are green.\n\nProcess note for the pause protocol: my standdown comment named this exact risk and named the\nrevision that must not be submitted, and it was submitted anyway. The record was correct and\nstill did not prevent it, which suggests a comment on a ticket is the wrong channel for \"do not\nsubmit X\" — a Gerrit -1 or a WIP flag on the change itself would have been enforceable. I will\nuse one of those next time rather than relying on a note the submitter may not read."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786644415462330001,"uuid":"8b9e881f-1aa0-455e-94c9-a39471ee991e"}